 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# Multiple issues with image handling and style properties in docx\n\nDescription\n\nWhen working with images and styles in docx, I've encountered several issues:\n\n1. When trying to add an image to a document, it fails completely. The image doesn't appear at all.\n\n2. Image dimensions are incorrect - width and height values seem to be swapped when inserting inline pictures.\n\n3. Style properties behave strangely - specifically when trying to set a style as semi-hidden, it doesn't work properly. The style remains visible when it should be hidden.\n\n4. Image height values are being negated or modified unexpectedly. When setting a specific height for an image, the actual height in the document is different.\n\nI've tried to create a simple reproduction script:\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\ndoc = Document()\ndoc.add_picture('image.png', width=2000000, height=3000000)\n# The image doesn't appear or has incorrect dimensions\n\nstyle = doc.styles['Normal']\nstyle.hidden = True\n# The style remains visible when it should be hidden\n\ndoc.save('test.docx')\n```\n\nThe URI for pictures also seems to be incorrect, which might be causing compatibility issues with some Word versions.\n</issue>\n",
